This notice covers the four demo games and only them: Meadow Run, Courtyard Key,
Trail Duel and Neon Rift. They are NOT covered by the MIT License in the root
LICENSE file, which applies to the MicroEngine engine, its tools and samples.

Covered (the "Demo Games"):

  - games/MeadowRun/, games/CourtyardKey/, games/TrailDuel/, games/NeonRift/:
    source code, levels, maps, dialogue, characters, names, procedural art and
    music written in code, scripts, screenshots and documentation;
  - tests/MeadowRun.Tests/, tests/CourtyardKey.Tests/, tests/TrailDuel.Tests/,
    tests/NeonRift.Tests/;
  - the builds of those games, including the browser packages served on the
    MicroEngine website;

except the third-party files listed in each game's CREDITS.md (the image and
audio files under games/<Name>/Content/). Those files belong to their authors
and are distributed under their own licences, stated in CREDITS.md; this
notice claims no rights in them.

What you may do:

  - Read and study the Demo Games' code to learn how MicroEngine works, and
    view it and fork it on GitHub as GitHub's Terms of Service allow.
  - Build and run them on your own computer to learn and to test MicroEngine.
  - Play the published demos.
  - Use the concepts, techniques and general ideas they show in your own,
    original games. Ideas, genres and game mechanics are not owned by anyone.
  - Propose changes to them through pull requests to the MicroEngine
    repository.

What you may not do without written permission from the copyright holder:

  - Redistribute the Demo Games, whole or in substantial part, in source or
    built form, outside GitHub's fork feature.
  - Sell or otherwise commercialise them, or publish a game that is
    substantially the same as one of them under another name.
  - Reuse their characters, names, levels, story or original art and music in
    another game.

The MicroEngine engine code that the Demo Games use stays under the MIT
License, and the third-party files keep their own licences: this notice does
not restrict them.

